  "note": [
    "Every code database entry that carries a flag of the M9 contract (plan section 7.2, 7.16 #47 and #48): wordsAreData, axisWords, frame, or sets.speedLimit with its bound; since M10 (P10) also sets.tcp, tool centre point control on or off, and frameWithoutValues, the close a code makes when it is written without values. One list per database file, in file order, each row the members the file declares and what the four readers must answer for them. Written by WP9.2. Since the M10 review also pole ('set' on the circle centre, 'use' on the moves around it), call (a code that hands its words to another program as arguments) and shift (a code whose axis words shift or set the coordinate system); the four readers are unchanged by them.",
    "src/lib/data/codes/flags.test.ts holds the shipped files to this list (a flag cannot be dropped, added or changed without this file changing, and so a reviewer reading it) and holds the TypeScript readers to the answers; tests/python/test_code_flags.py holds gedit_nc.axis_words_of, frame_of, speed_limit_bound_of and tcp_of to the same answers.",
    "axisWords: 'data' = the axis words of the block are values, not positions (coordinate set, shift, centre, tilt angle, dwell time); 'machine' = positions outside the program's frame (machine coordinates, reference points). frame: 'open' / 'close' = the code opens or closes a coordinate frame that is not the program's own; a code whose values decide is 'open'. speedLimitBound: 'upper' is the clamp every speed limit was before M9; 'lower' is a minimum. tcp (P10, decision of 2026-10-04): 'on' / 'off' = the code switches tool centre point control, under which X, Y and Z are the tool tip in the workpiece; it is never a frame (TRAORI lost its frame: 'open' at P10). frameWithoutValues (P10): 'close' = written without values (CYCLE800(), TRANS or ROT alone) the code closes the frames of its group; with any value it reads as frame says. frameZeroWords (owner decision of 2026-10-08, M10-2): the angle words of a tilt that reads as none when every one of them is zero (Klartext cycle 19, PLANE SPATIAL, PROJECTED and EULER); a block that writes none of them changes no frame, and an angle not written keeps its value. frameEmptyCloses (M12.5, B-3): a block of the tilt that writes none of those words and carries this sub-block (Klartext CYCL DEF 19.1 with no angle) closes the frames of its group; 19.0 changes nothing. Read by the modal interpreter only; the four readers are unchanged by it.",
    "droppedByOverride lists the entries a child database replaces with an entry that carries fewer flags than the entry it replaced, each with the reason. An override that drops a flag without a row here fails the test."
  ],
